WEBVTT

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:03.720
Think about the next email you need to write.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.160
ChatGPT can help you get a clear first draft,

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.680
fast.

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.030
In this course, every example is invented.

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:14.810
You'll learn how to ask... and then how to check.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.940
Before you open a chat, write down what the task is for.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.920
A short reminder email is a great place to start,

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.680
because you can check every detail against a few notes.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.930
Open ChatGPT in your browser, and use the account your

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:36.930
business approves. If you have a work workspace,

00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:39.230
check that you're actually in it.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:43.200
Keep real client and staff details out of practice chats.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:46.960
In our invented office, the notes just say a visitor needs

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.260
an appointment reminder.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:51.620
The name and the time stay as placeholders.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:56.330
Now, plans. Free is enough for this course's core

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:01.570
exercises. Go, Plus and Pro are personal paid plans.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:04.120
Business is a managed team workspace,

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.900
and Enterprise adds more advanced organisation controls.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.300
Choose by need, and check the current plan page.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:14.110
Jot down a quick account checklist:

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:16.790
the service, the workspace you'll use,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.850
and who can answer your questions.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.490
Not sure you have permission?

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:23.810
Pause the real task, and keep practising with the invented

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:24.890
one.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.480
On a personal account, open Settings,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.400
then Data controls, and review Improve the model for

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:33.520
everyone.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:36.570
Turning it off stops new conversations being used for

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.010
training. It doesn't delete your chat history,

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.150
and it doesn't make confidential information okay to

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:43.290
upload.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.320
One catch. If you give thumbs up or thumbs down feedback,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.320
that conversation may still be used for training,

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.540
even after you opt out.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.170
Review Memory under Personalization too.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.550
For practice, try a Temporary chat,

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:01.290
and choose Unpersonalized if it's offered.

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.490
Temporary doesn't mean instant deletion.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.840
Then write the prompt.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.620
Give only the details the draft needs.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.340
Ask for a subject line and a short message,

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.240
and keep missing details in square brackets.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:18.420
Don't ask it to guess what a client meant.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.470
Read the result beside your notes.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.250
Look for an added attachment, a new deadline,

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.930
or a claim that something's already agreed.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:31.210
A warmer tone only helps if the meaning stays the same.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:34.860
Now try the reception notice in the next lesson.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.000
Check the times, and watch for added promises.

00:02:38.020 --> 00:02:40.780
Keep a note of what you changed, so you can explain the

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.060
draft to whoever reviews it.

00:02:43.230 --> 00:02:46.842
The goal is a clear, checked message that you understand,

00:02:46.862 --> 00:02:48.219
and can stand behind.

00:02:48.239 --> 00:02:51.037
This is independent training from The Colab.

00:02:51.057 --> 00:02:53.729
We're not affiliated with, or endorsed by,

00:02:53.749 --> 00:02:54.930
OpenAI.
